  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision for Protection, Emergency Shelter and Non-Food Items benefiting conflict affected populations in Hirshabelle and Galmudug states</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this $3.23m UNHCR project is to provide emergency shelter and protection response to conflict induced IDPs and host community members. To that end, UNHCR will provide emergency shelter kits through cash and in-kind non-food item (NFI) kits (blankets, mats, kitchen sets, lamps, mosquito nets, etc.) as well as cash for NFI kits. In addition, UNHCR will conduct refresher trainings on protection, establish protection desks and deploy mobile protection teams, and provide protection minimum service response. In total, UNHCR will reach 78,000 people through the shelter and NFI component, including 13,756 women and 25,739 girls, and 34,700 people through the protection component, including 6,120 women and 11,451 girls.</narrative>
  </description>
